<title>FRANCE: Marseille top French regional airport for airfreight.</title>
<headline>Marseille top French regional airport for airfreight.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's top ten regional airports for flown airfreight in January 1997, with percentage change on January 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>			     Tonnes    Pct change</p>
<p>					   against Jan 96</p>
<p> 1  Marseille	    3,805     up    9.6</p>
<p> 2  Basle-Mulhouse*    2, 959    down  9.0</p>
<p> 3  Toulouse	     2,101     down  2.0</p>
<p> 4  Lyon-Satolas	 1,790     up    2.9</p>
<p> 5  Lille **	     1,771     up    5.0</p>
<p> 6  Nice		   1,356     up    8.2</p>
<p> 7  Bordeaux		 649     up   10.0</p>
<p> 8  Montpellier	    448     up   17.3</p>
<p> 9  Strasbourg	     424     down 23.4</p>
<p> 10 Rennes		   329     up   69.4</p>
<p>*  Includes traffic handled in Swiss zone of airport.</p>
<p>** Also includes trucked air freight</p>
<p>The figures do not include France's major gateways for airfreight, Paris.CDG and Paris/Orly.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
